{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39649262",
      "title": "Module Summary",
      "sourceHash": "e8419c4fd929366e85d7937b0c2f093ea2ba58f5c04f7e2db56671bb816ffab7",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0,
          "end": 1.68,
          "en": "So that's it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 1.68,
          "end": 4.461,
          "en": "for this React Essentials section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.461,
          "end": 9.42,
          "en": "And in this section we built this beautiful,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.42,
          "end": 13.89,
          "en": "interactive demo web app here with React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.89,
          "end": 15.78,
          "en": "And whilst building it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.78,
          "end": 18.55,
          "en": "we learned about all these core concepts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.55,
          "end": 21.797,
          "en": "which you also see on this demo website.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.797,
          "end": 25.89,
          "en": "You learned that React is all about components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.89,
          "end": 28.267,
          "en": "and you learned how you can create",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.267,
          "end": 31.601,
          "en": "and also use such components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.601,
          "end": 35.76,
          "en": "that components are in the end simply functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.76,
          "end": 37.02,
          "en": "which must have a name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.02,
          "end": 39.844,
          "en": "that starts with an uppercase character,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.844,
          "end": 44.614,
          "en": "and which must return a value that can be rendered by React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.614,
          "end": 49.524,
          "en": "which typically means that they return on JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.524,
          "end": 53.88,
          "en": "And you learned that you can use these component functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.88,
          "end": 56.43,
          "en": "pretty much as if they were custom",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.43,
          "end": 59.763,
          "en": "HTML elements inside of JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.893,
          "end": 65.68299999999999,
          "en": "You also learned how to configure components with props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 65.68299999999999,
          "end": 68.672,
          "en": "like this isSelected prop here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 68.672,
          "end": 71.82,
          "en": "that you can set any props you want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 71.82,
          "end": 76.44,
          "en": "or even spread an entire object as key value pairs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 76.44,
          "end": 80.1,
          "en": "so as props onto a component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 80.1,
          "end": 82.14,
          "en": "and that inside of a component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 82.14,
          "end": 85.62,
          "en": "you then get those props as the first parameter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 85.62,
          "end": 87.63,
          "en": "in that component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 87.63,
          "end": 91.42099999999999,
          "en": "And you can use object destructuring if you want to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 91.42099999999999,
          "end": 94.74000000000001,
          "en": "to get hold of these different props like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 94.74000000000001,
          "end": 99.47999999999999,
          "en": "Alternatively, you could use props and then props.image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 99.47999999999999,
          "end": 102.12299999999999,
          "en": "props.title, and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 103.77000000000001,
          "end": 106.064,
          "en": "But with that, we of course only got started,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 106.064,
          "end": 109.179,
          "en": "because you also learned how to output dynamic content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 109.179,
          "end": 111.66,
          "en": "with those curly braces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 111.66,
          "end": 115.32,
          "en": "And you can either output content between tags",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 115.32,
          "end": 118.718,
          "en": "or as attribute values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 118.718,
          "end": 122.85,
          "en": "And you learned about the special children prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 122.85,
          "end": 127.68,
          "en": "which is a prop created and provided by React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 127.68,
          "end": 130.98,
          "en": "which simply gives you access to the content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 130.98,
          "end": 133.47,
          "en": "that's passed to your component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 133.47,
          "end": 138.06,
          "en": "between your component's opening and closing tags.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 138.06,
          "end": 142.02,
          "en": "So this content here between those tags is received",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 142.02,
          "end": 146.598,
          "en": "inside of the component through that special children prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 146.598,
          "end": 151.14,
          "en": "So components and props and JSX code, as you learned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 151.14,
          "end": 154.341,
          "en": "are all super important features,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 154.341,
          "end": 159.21,
          "en": "but if you only had those features, you would not be able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 159.21,
          "end": 161.523,
          "en": "to build interactive websites.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 162.48,
          "end": 166.74,
          "en": "For that, instead, you also must be able to listen to events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 166.74,
          "end": 171.159,
          "en": "which you can do with these special on props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 171.159,
          "end": 175.11,
          "en": "And you also learned how you can add your own on props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 175.11,
          "end": 178.44,
          "en": "to your own components so that you can receive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 178.44,
          "end": 181.71,
          "en": "and forward functions to the actual elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 181.71,
          "end": 184.8,
          "en": "that should register event handlers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 184.8,
          "end": 186.84,
          "en": "So here, for example, this TabButton",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 186.84,
          "end": 189.967,
          "en": "has the onSelect prop, which is used as a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 189.967,
          "end": 193.35,
          "en": "for the onClick prop on the built-in button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 193.35,
          "end": 198.24,
          "en": "And we can use this onSelect prop to point at the function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 198.24,
          "end": 200.79,
          "en": "that should be executed when the button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 200.79,
          "end": 204.06,
          "en": "inside of that TabButton is clicked in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 204.06,
          "end": 206.7,
          "en": "But of course, this alone is not enough.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 206.7,
          "end": 209.88,
          "en": "You also learned that if you want to update the UI",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 209.88,
          "end": 214.88,
          "en": "you must useState, this special useState hook to be precise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 216.42000000000002,
          "end": 220.62,
          "en": "You can use this hook to register some data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 220.62,
          "end": 224.85,
          "en": "that's managed by React and to update that data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 224.85,
          "end": 228.96,
          "en": "with help of that special state updating function here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 228.96,
          "end": 232.095,
          "en": "And this feature here, this useState hook,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 232.095,
          "end": 236.034,
          "en": "therefore allows you to manage and update data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 236.034,
          "end": 241.034,
          "en": "which when updated will cause the component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 241.17,
          "end": 244.563,
          "en": "to which the state belongs to execute again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 244.563,
          "end": 248.79,
          "en": "so that the JSX code is also reevaluated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 248.79,
          "end": 252.72,
          "en": "and the UI is updated if needed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 252.72,
          "end": 254.97,
          "en": "So React will basically take a look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 254.97,
          "end": 258.845,
          "en": "at the old JSX code and the new JSX code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 258.845,
          "end": 262.71,
          "en": "and if it finds any differences, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 262.71,
          "end": 265.71,
          "en": "because this tab content changed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 265.71,
          "end": 269.631,
          "en": "because here the data that should be output changed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 269.631,
          "end": 274.59000000000003,
          "en": "React will go ahead and update the actual UI",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 274.59000000000003,
          "end": 277.35,
          "en": "to match our new state again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 277.35,
          "end": 281.22,
          "en": "Now along the way in this section, you also learned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 281.22,
          "end": 285.33,
          "en": "about different ways of outputting conditional content,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 285.33,
          "end": 289.5,
          "en": "for example, by using a variable and an if statement,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 289.5,
          "end": 291.69,
          "en": "and by then outputting that variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 291.69,
          "end": 295.53,
          "en": "as dynamic content in your JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 295.53,
          "end": 298.17,
          "en": "But you also learned about alternatives",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 298.17,
          "end": 300.5,
          "en": "like using a ternary expression",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 300.5,
          "end": 305.5,
          "en": "or by using the logical and operator as a shortcut.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 305.52,
          "end": 306.912,
          "en": "And last but not least,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 306.912,
          "end": 311.26,
          "en": "you learned how to output list data dynamically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 311.26,
          "end": 314.312,
          "en": "by mapping an array of data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 314.312,
          "end": 319.312,
          "en": "with the built-in map method into an array of JSX elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 320.259,
          "end": 323.1,
          "en": "The special thing to keep in mind here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 323.1,
          "end": 326.651,
          "en": "just is that you then also must add such a key prop here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 326.651,
          "end": 330.603,
          "en": "so that behind the scenes React is able to render",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 330.603,
          "end": 333.81,
          "en": "and update that list efficiently.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 333.81,
          "end": 338.81,
          "en": "And with that, you now get a solid set of React Essentials,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 339.45,
          "end": 341.15999999999997,
          "en": "essentials which you will need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 341.15999999999997,
          "end": 345.21,
          "en": "in basically any React app you are going to build.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 345.21,
          "end": 348.45,
          "en": "And you are therefore now ready to get started",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 348.45,
          "end": 351.45,
          "en": "building your first basic React apps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 351.45,
          "end": 354.99,
          "en": "And then of course also to dive much deeper",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 354.99,
          "end": 356.4,
          "en": "into those essentials,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 356.4,
          "end": 359.67,
          "en": "but also into React and advanced features.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 359.67,
          "end": 360.54,
          "en": "And of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 360.54,
          "end": 363.813,
          "en": "we're going to do all these things in this course.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}